\"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a94c3e4cb7b3a20f127de9fff6fd6211b88f8aa11923cbfc63bee291fe874b12","event_uuid":"48ce743e-800e-44b4-99a6-8ad359d42815","position":{"commit_sha":"561b2495f0a37f96f83d4e4af514775da873cbe1","position":"1787175985345362001-48ce743e-800e-44b4-99a6-8ad359d42815"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f18596c4e56f9d33173e9a85dbb15fee73289dbc41820f9241435cab31318c63","event_uuid":"75e9a334-9541-4aba-9435-0fc5ba499dc6","position":{"commit_sha":"6351a51ae2ab1ed70c8c4ffb4befbff12fb2ff90","position":"1787175991390143001-75e9a334-9541-4aba-9435-0fc5ba499dc6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0224f85dd07d923068868d57d9bd487a3ac198fc2d642782d14e0510c5fc0050","event_uuid":"8f1d4adb-1d95-4696-ba2f-5ee8c0a70255","position":{"commit_sha":"545aabcc8a6f37439b890df75a49f767985df1dd","position":"1787175992951309001-8f1d4adb-1d95-4696-ba2f-5ee8c0a70255"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## /rebar-debug RCA — investigated, AC#1+AC#4 delivered, AC#2 rests on a false premise\n\n**Confirmed mechanism (defect, as the ticket states).** The idempotency oracle froze\n`_now_iso` only on `binding_store`. RP-02 S2 T2 moved the absence/tombstone/comment\ncluster (`clear_absent` + siblings) into `binding_lifecycle`, which resolves its OWN\nmodule-level `_now_iso` (binding_lifecycle.py:45; `clear_absent` at :296 stamps via it).\nSo the freeze no longer reaches those moved ops. **Fix (AC#1):** freeze BOTH module\nclocks. Delivered + verified (idempotency file 3/3 green, no regression).\n\n**AC#4 audit (done):** the only `binding_store_mod`-targeted patch of a moved subject in\n`test_reconcile_idempotency.py` is the `_now_iso` freeze at line 311. No other moved-subject\npatches exist. Clean.\n\n**AC#2 is NOT satisfiable through this integration test — verified at runtime, not assumed.**\nAC#2 asks: with the patch in place, seeding an unconditional `clear_absent` stamp must drive\n`test_reconcile_idempotency.py` RED. It cannot, for two independently sufficient reasons:\n\n1. **`clear_absent` is never reached on a healthy in-window pass.** Its only two call sites —\n   `binding_walk.py:254` (`persist and obs.state is PRESENT and jira_key not in curr_snapshot`)\n   and `outbound_differ.py:675` (bound-but-absent key whose direct GET returns 200) — are\n   BOTH gated on an *out-of-window-but-alive* key. The idempotency fixture seeds all keys\n   in-window, so `clear_absent` does not run. Proof: instrumented entry trace over both\n   passes shows **zero** `clear_absent` calls; a seeded unconditional-stamp mutation left the\n   test GREEN.\n2. **Even forcing a key out-of-window, the differ's direct GET does not hit the in-process\n   fake.** The fetch uses `fetcher._load_acli` (the fake), but the bound-but-absent GET uses\n   `run_differs._load_reconcile_backend()` → `select_backend(compose_config())`, a\n   config-resolved REAL backend whose `.transport` 404s for a synthetic key. So a forced\n   out-of-window `DIG-1` takes the 404 → `note_absent_or_rekey` path, never `clear_absent`.\n   Proof: with an added `out_of_window` fake mechanism, the differ selected `DIG-1` for a GET\n   (`SELECTED={'DIG-1'}`) but `_safe_get_issue` returned `_DELETED` (404) and the fake's\n   `get_issue_by_rest` was never called.\n\nThe `clear_absent` no-stamp contract is already pinned at unit tier:\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence`\n(the ticket's own Impact note acknowledges this containment). The AC#2 premise — that a\nhealthy idempotent pass exercises `clear_absent` — is factually wrong for this test.\n\n**Recommendation (for user/reviewer).** Either (a) accept AC#1 hardening + the existing\nunit-tier guard as sufficient and drop/reclassify AC#2; or (b) if an integration-tier\nmutation-RED is still wanted, it requires a harness extension that wires the fake into the\nBackend port (`.transport` + `.outbound`/`.inbound` mappers) AND an out-of-window fixture so\nthe bound-but-absent-alive path executes — that is a test-harness story of its own, larger\nthan this follow-up's framing. Filing as a follow-up is the recommended path if (b) is\ndesired.","timestamp":1787164346002065001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Close disposition (force, operator judgment)\n\nAC#1 + AC#4 delivered and landed via Gerrit change 1911 (commit dc2e799bd3, MERGED to main). AC#2 rests on a proven FALSE PREMISE: `clear_absent` is structurally unreachable on a healthy in-window pass, so its seeded unconditional-stamp mutation cannot drive the integration test RED (documented in the RCA comment above; the completion verifier independently confirmed the mutation leaves the test GREEN). Operator-attesting AC#2 as met would be dishonest and was withdrawn.\n\nResidual harness gap filed as story 6045-bdf3-ddad-4461 (deiform-filmable-akitainu), linked discovered_from this bug. Closing via --force because the blocking criterion is invalid (false premise), not incomplete — force records no signed completion attestation, which is the correct honest signal here.","timestamp":1787175985345362001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"AC#2 is a proven false premise (clear_absent unreachable in-window); AC#1/AC#4 landed via Gerrit 1911; residual harness gap filed as 6045\". Session: f26be6be45.","timestamp":1787175992951309001}],"created_at":1787123662531556001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ca636da4-c6ad-4232-9a62-4789dd9f9671","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f59b-56c1-596d-422a"},{"link_uuid":"1ad975da-1d56-4eaf-80af-0c599f6fec2e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0b07-f245-3423-47ca"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py:311` patches `binding_store_mod._now_iso` to advance the wall clock, then asserts that an unchanged second reconcile pass rewrites no bytes. The patch is how the test proves the no-churn contract is real rather than a coincidence of a fast test run.\n\nRP-02 S2 T2 moved the absence/tombstone/comment cluster into `binding_lifecycle.py`, so `clear_absent` (and its siblings) now resolve `_now_iso` from `binding_lifecycle`, not `binding_store`. The existing patch therefore no longer reaches them.\n\n## Impact\nThe test still PASSES, and correctly so — the no-churn contract means the clock is never consulted on a healthy pass. But its blast radius narrowed: it would no longer catch a regression that made `clear_absent` (or another moved operation) stamp `updated_at` unconditionally. That is a silent weakening of an integration-tier oracle.\n\nCoverage did not disappear, it moved tiers: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py::test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence` pins the contract directly on the policy owner, and was one of the held-out tests for S2 T2. So the risk here is contained, which is why this is a follow-up rather than a blocker.\n\n## Outcome\nRestore the integration oracle's original reach by patching the clock on BOTH modules, so it again fails if any binding operation stamps a timestamp on an unchanged pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The idempotency test patches `_now_iso` on `binding_lifecycle` as well as `binding_store` (or on a single shared source, if one is introduced).\n- [x] With the patch in place, making `clear_absent` stamp `updated_at` unconditionally drives the integration test RED — verified by seeding that mutation, not assumed.\n- [x] The test still passes unmutated, and still asserts byte-level no-churn across an unchanged second pass.\n- [x] Audit the same file for other `binding_store_mod`-targeted patches whose subject moved to `binding_lifecycle.py` during RP-02 S2.\n\n## Notes\nDiscovered by the implementation subagent during RP-02 S2 T2 and deliberately left alone there: that ticket's instructions forbade touching test files outside its scope, and widening an integration oracle is a test-hygiene change that deserves its own review rather than riding along in an extraction slice.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","force_close_reason":"AC#2 is a proven false premise (clear_absent unreachable in-window); AC#1/AC#4 landed via Gerrit 1911; residual harness gap filed as 6045","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0b07-f245-3423-47ca"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"75e9a334-9541-4aba-9435-0fc5ba499dc6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["reconciler","tests","janitor"],"ticket_id":"02c4-4e64-5ee3-459c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Idempotency oracle no longer reaches moved binding clock reads","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fe9c70b8-210a-434c-aab6-5742225d3e22","b49de016-7fb7-482c-a51c-9bd8e465c198","de5485ae-f5c9-4ef8-a1c2-a8d7ac7d56b8","9b9aa5db-8807-4e10-9521-e4fd9df49ae3","1ad975da-1d56-4eaf-80af-0c599f6fec2e","fddc4757-4179-44c6-9649-eac53e9a1222","5d1001ea-0e73-4c72-82b8-c88b907848a4","3ce3bd72-a7d1-4d5a-b057-3f399d7d3e2e","48ce743e-800e-44b4-99a6-8ad359d42815","75e9a334-9541-4aba-9435-0fc5ba499dc6","8f1d4adb-1d95-4696-ba2f-5ee8c0a70255"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787178579097688001,"uuid":"fc94c9d3-7f1f-4080-9319-60418d20595a"}